            <div xml:id="d73">

                <pb facs="0107" n="97" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg97"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.796/2–1848: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-02-18T11:00:00+08:00">February 18,
                            1948—11 a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 17—11:41 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>367. Since publicity might have unfortunate repercussions, Consulate General will
                    be discreet in disseminating information contained in last sentence Deptel 288,
                    February 16, unless further instructed by Department or Embassy.</p>
                <p>Sent Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
